Degraded Operation Manager

Copyright © Summon Software Labs

Degraded Operation Manager is an open-source, vendor-neutral runtime for governing facility-wide degraded operating modes: it decides which mode is authoritative from the current incidents, failure domains, capacity, redundancy, power, cooling, maintenance, policy and protected obligations, what service that mode still permits, what it must restrict, and what evidence is required to leave it.

